IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ia-types`

-- Insurance Act 1966 — GOAL 4: WHAT A CONTRAVENTION CAN COST
-- (every penalty in the Act; ss 142-145).
--
--   "For this offence, committed by an individual or by a corporation, what
--    is the most the court may fine, imprison for, and add for each day it
--    continues; and for how much may the Authority compound it?"
--
-- The Act states two kinds of penalty. Most offences open to anyone give
-- one figure for "an individual" and another for "any other case" (the
-- `split` rows). The rest give one figure for whoever is convicted (the
-- `single` rows); s 143 then lets the court fine a corporation up to twice
-- that, unless the duty falls only on corporations (licensed insurers,
-- authorised reinsurers and registered brokers are all bodies corporate:
-- ss 11(3), 77(1)). Imprisonment is in years (12 months = 1).
-- Source: ../source/IA1966.txt, the penalty limb of each section listed.

§ `Goal 4 — penalties`

DECLARE `IA offence` IS ONE OF
    `s 4(5) carrying on insurance business, or providing reinsurance, unlicensed`
    `s 5(2) holding out as a licensed insurer or authorised reinsurer`
    `s 6(7) using the word "insurance" without entitlement`
    `s 8(3) soliciting for an insurer not entitled, or for business outside Singapore`
    `s 9(8) operating an unregistered representative office`
    `s 10(2) refusing to submit books for examination`
    `s 26(6) obtaining effective control without approval, or breaching its conditions`
    `s 27(7) becoming a substantial shareholder, or a 5% arrangement, without approval`
    `s 27(8) breaching a condition of approval under s 27`
    `s 28(6) failing to comply with a notice of objection`
    `s 29(4) failing to comply with a direction on shares`
    `s 32(4) failing to provide shareholder information, or giving false information`
    `s 33A(8) breaching the Minister's condition`
    `s 39(5) false web aggregator information, wilfully`
    `s 39(5) false web aggregator information, not wilfully`
    `s 62(2) holding out as a foreign insurer or its agent`
    `s 98(4) failing to produce documents on inspection`
    `s 101(5) disclosing an inspection report`
    `s 101(6) receiving a report knowing it was disclosed in breach (s 142(3))`
    `s 102(7) failing to comply with the Authority's direction`
    `s 114(2) failing to comply with an order to assist a foreign authority`
    `s 114(3) false material or statement to assist a foreign authority`
    `s 126(2) contravening winding-up regulations`
    `s 142(2) false document or information without due care`
    `s 142(3) breach of a duty with no penalty expressly provided`
    `s 154(3) contravening regulations`
    `s 7(2) co-branding without consent`
    `s 11(10) breaching a licence condition`
    `s 11(11) failing the prescribed financial requirements`
    `s 17(6) failing fund solvency or capital adequacy`
    `s 19(4) failing the custody rules for documents of title`
    `s 20(4) failing to maintain assets in Singapore`
    `s 22(4) issuing a policy at a premium not approved by the actuary (each occasion)`
    `s 23(6) using a prohibited form or brochure, or no warning`
    `s 24(6) paying financial advisers' remuneration otherwise than as permitted`
    `s 34(8) acquiring or holding a major stake without approval`
    `s 35(16) lacking a required officer, or appointing without approval`
    `s 35(17) failing to remove an officer as directed`
    `s 36(2) permitting a disqualified person to act`
    `s 39(4) failing to provide web aggregator information`
    `s 39(7) failing to take reasonable care over web aggregator information`
    `s 41(3) failing to manufacture and offer a directed life policy`
    `s 42(8) breaching a condition of authorisation`
    `s 48(4) an authorised reinsurer failing to maintain assets in Singapore`
    `s 54(10) an administrator failing to remove an officer`
    `s 58(7) a foreign insurer's agent failing to remove an officer`
    `s 64(7) arranging as agent without a written agreement`
    `s 67(3) failing pre-contract disclosure`
    `s 69(5) misrepresentation by an intermediary with intent to deceive`
    `s 70(2) acting as agent for an insurer not entitled`
    `s 71(5) using a prohibited written communication`
    `s 75(2) carrying on broking unregistered`
    `s 78(2) breaching a condition of registration as a broker`
    `s 82(6) failing to keep insurance broking premium accounts`
    `s 83(3) placing risk with an unlicensed insurer`
    `s 86(3) volume-based remuneration`
    `s 87(4) agreeing to take control of a broker without approval`
    `s 88(8) a broker failing to remove an officer`
    `s 89(3) a broker's unsecured loan over the limit`
    `s 90(2) holding out as a registered insurance broker`
    `s 91(4) using the words "insurance broking"`
    `s 92(9) an exempt broker breaching a condition`
    `s 97(6) failing to lodge accounts or actuarial reports (ss 94, 95)`
    `s 100(5) refusing a parent supervisor access`
    `s 101C(5) disclosing an investigation report`
    `s 101C(6) receiving an investigation report knowing it was disclosed in breach`
    `s 101R(1) a solicitor failing to name a privileged communicant`
    `s 101R(2) failing an examination, entry or warrant requirement`
    `s 101R(3) failing to sign the record or keep copy conditions`
    `s 101R(4) failing to produce books under s 101L`
    `s 101R(5) false information in an investigation`
    `s 101R(7) concealing or destroying books under investigation`
    `s 101R(8) obstructing the Authority`
    `s 101R(9) an occupier failing to give facilities`
    `s 103(10) acting after an appointment is revoked under statutory management`
    `s 105(2) failing to give information to a statutory manager`
    `s 119(4) a transferee failing a direction on the auditor's statement`
    `s 124(2) failing to give information under Part 3AA`

DECLARE `Penalty schedule` HAS
    `individual fine`                IS A NUMBER
    `individual imprisonment, years` IS A NUMBER
    `individual fine per day continuing` IS A NUMBER
    `other fine`                     IS A NUMBER
    `other fine per day continuing`  IS A NUMBER
    `split by the person`            IS A BOOLEAN   -- the Act prescribes different penalties for individuals and others
    `a duty only on corporations`    IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 143(2)(a), 142(5)

DECLARE `IA penalty` HAS
    `fine`                           IS A NUMBER
    `imprisonment, years`            IS A NUMBER
    `fine per day continuing after conviction` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER, c IS A NUMBER, d IS A NUMBER, e IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Penalty schedule`
`split` a b c d e MEANS `Penalty schedule` OF a, b, c, d, e, TRUE, FALSE

GIVEN f IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER, dd IS A NUMBER, corp IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Penalty schedule`
`single` f y dd corp MEANS `Penalty schedule` OF f, y, dd, f, dd, FALSE, corp

§§ `The penalty each section prescribes`

-- `split`  individual: fine, years, per day;   any other case: fine, per day
-- `single` fine, years, per day, a duty only on corporations
@ref ss 4-11, 17-24, 26-29, 32-42, 48, 54, 58, 62, 64-75, 78, 82-92, 97-105, 114, 119, 124, 126, 142, 154
GIVEN o IS AN `IA offence`
GIVETH A `Penalty schedule`
`the penalty schedule for` o MEANS
    CONSIDER o
    WHEN `s 4(5) carrying on insurance business, or providing reinsurance, unlicensed`       THEN `split` 125000 3 12500 250000 25000
    WHEN `s 5(2) holding out as a licensed insurer or authorised reinsurer`                  THEN `split` 125000 3 12500 250000 25000
    WHEN `s 6(7) using the word "insurance" without entitlement`                             THEN `split`  12500 1  1250  25000  2500
    WHEN `s 8(3) soliciting for an insurer not entitled, or for business outside Singapore`  THEN `split` 125000 3 12500 250000 25000
    WHEN `s 9(8) operating an unregistered representative office`                            THEN `split`  50000 2  5000 100000 10000
    WHEN `s 10(2) refusing to submit books for examination`                                  THEN `split`  50000 2  5000 100000 10000
    WHEN `s 26(6) obtaining effective control without approval, or breaching its conditions` THEN `split` 125000 3 12500 250000 25000
    WHEN `s 27(7) becoming a substantial shareholder, or a 5% arrangement, without approval` THEN `split` 125000 0 12500 250000 25000
    WHEN `s 27(8) breaching a condition of approval under s 27`                              THEN `split` 125000 3 12500 250000 25000
    WHEN `s 28(6) failing to comply with a notice of objection`                              THEN `split` 125000 3 12500 250000 25000
    WHEN `s 29(4) failing to comply with a direction on shares`                              THEN `split` 125000 3 12500 250000 25000
    WHEN `s 32(4) failing to provide shareholder information, or giving false information`   THEN `split` 125000 3 12500 250000 25000
    WHEN `s 33A(8) breaching the Minister's condition`                                       THEN `split` 125000 3 12500 250000 25000
    WHEN `s 39(5) false web aggregator information, wilfully`                                THEN `split` 125000 3     0 250000     0
    WHEN `s 39(5) false web aggregator information, not wilfully`                            THEN `split` 125000 0     0 250000     0
    WHEN `s 62(2) holding out as a foreign insurer or its agent`                             THEN `split`  50000 2  5000 100000 10000
    WHEN `s 98(4) failing to produce documents on inspection`                                THEN `split`  50000 2  5000 100000 10000
    WHEN `s 101(5) disclosing an inspection report`                                          THEN `split` 125000 3     0 250000     0
    WHEN `s 101(6) receiving a report knowing it was disclosed in breach (s 142(3))`         THEN `split`  50000 2  5000 100000 10000
    WHEN `s 102(7) failing to comply with the Authority's direction`                         THEN `split` 125000 3 12500 250000 25000
    WHEN `s 114(2) failing to comply with an order to assist a foreign authority`            THEN `split`  50000 2  5000 100000 10000
    WHEN `s 114(3) false material or statement to assist a foreign authority`                THEN `split`  50000 2     0 100000     0
    WHEN `s 126(2) contravening winding-up regulations`                                      THEN `split` 125000 3 12500 250000 25000
    WHEN `s 142(2) false document or information without due care`                           THEN `split` 125000 3     0 250000     0
    WHEN `s 142(3) breach of a duty with no penalty expressly provided`                      THEN `split`  50000 2  5000 100000 10000
    WHEN `s 154(3) contravening regulations`                                                 THEN `split`  50000 2  5000 100000 10000
    WHEN `s 7(2) co-branding without consent`                                                THEN `single` 100000 0 10000 TRUE 
    WHEN `s 11(10) breaching a licence condition`                                            THEN `single` 100000 0 10000 TRUE 
    WHEN `s 11(11) failing the prescribed financial requirements`                            THEN `single` 250000 0 25000 TRUE 
    WHEN `s 17(6) failing fund solvency or capital adequacy`                                 THEN `single` 250000 0 25000 TRUE 
    WHEN `s 19(4) failing the custody rules for documents of title`                          THEN `single`  12500 0  1250 FALSE
    WHEN `s 20(4) failing to maintain assets in Singapore`                                   THEN `single` 250000 0 25000 TRUE 
    WHEN `s 22(4) issuing a policy at a premium not approved by the actuary (each occasion)` THEN `single`  25000 0     0 TRUE 
    WHEN `s 23(6) using a prohibited form or brochure, or no warning`                        THEN `single`  25000 0  2500 TRUE 
    WHEN `s 24(6) paying financial advisers' remuneration otherwise than as permitted`       THEN `single`  25000 0  2500 TRUE 
    WHEN `s 34(8) acquiring or holding a major stake without approval`                       THEN `single` 250000 0 25000 TRUE 
    WHEN `s 35(16) lacking a required officer, or appointing without approval`               THEN `single` 100000 0 10000 TRUE 
    WHEN `s 35(17) failing to remove an officer as directed`                                 THEN `single` 250000 0     0 TRUE 
    WHEN `s 36(2) permitting a disqualified person to act`                                   THEN `single` 250000 0 25000 TRUE 
    WHEN `s 39(4) failing to provide web aggregator information`                             THEN `single` 100000 0 10000 TRUE 
    WHEN `s 39(7) failing to take reasonable care over web aggregator information`           THEN `single`  25000 0     0 TRUE 
    WHEN `s 41(3) failing to manufacture and offer a directed life policy`                   THEN `single` 100000 0 10000 TRUE 
    WHEN `s 42(8) breaching a condition of authorisation`                                    THEN `single` 100000 0 10000 TRUE 
    WHEN `s 48(4) an authorised reinsurer failing to maintain assets in Singapore`           THEN `single` 250000 0 25000 TRUE 
    WHEN `s 54(10) an administrator failing to remove an officer`                            THEN `single` 250000 0     0 FALSE
    WHEN `s 58(7) a foreign insurer's agent failing to remove an officer`                    THEN `single` 250000 0     0 FALSE
    WHEN `s 64(7) arranging as agent without a written agreement`                            THEN `single`  25000 1  2500 FALSE
    WHEN `s 67(3) failing pre-contract disclosure`                                           THEN `single`  25000 1     0 FALSE
    WHEN `s 69(5) misrepresentation by an intermediary with intent to deceive`               THEN `single`  50000 1     0 FALSE
    WHEN `s 70(2) acting as agent for an insurer not entitled`                               THEN `single`  25000 3     0 FALSE
    WHEN `s 71(5) using a prohibited written communication`                                  THEN `single`  25000 1     0 FALSE
    WHEN `s 75(2) carrying on broking unregistered`                                          THEN `single`  75000 3  7500 FALSE
    WHEN `s 78(2) breaching a condition of registration as a broker`                         THEN `single`  50000 0  5000 TRUE 
    WHEN `s 82(6) failing to keep insurance broking premium accounts`                        THEN `single` 100000 0     0 TRUE 
    WHEN `s 83(3) placing risk with an unlicensed insurer`                                   THEN `single`  25000 3     0 FALSE
    WHEN `s 86(3) volume-based remuneration`                                                 THEN `single`  50000 1  5000 FALSE
    WHEN `s 87(4) agreeing to take control of a broker without approval`                     THEN `single`  25000 2     0 FALSE
    WHEN `s 88(8) a broker failing to remove an officer`                                     THEN `single` 150000 0     0 TRUE 
    WHEN `s 89(3) a broker's unsecured loan over the limit`                                  THEN `single`  12500 0  1250 TRUE 
    WHEN `s 90(2) holding out as a registered insurance broker`                              THEN `single`  50000 1  5000 FALSE
    WHEN `s 91(4) using the words "insurance broking"`                                       THEN `single`  12500 0  1250 FALSE
    WHEN `s 92(9) an exempt broker breaching a condition`                                    THEN `single`  12500 0  1250 FALSE
    WHEN `s 97(6) failing to lodge accounts or actuarial reports (ss 94, 95)`                THEN `single` 100000 0 10000 TRUE 
    WHEN `s 100(5) refusing a parent supervisor access`                                      THEN `single` 100000 0 10000 TRUE 
    WHEN `s 101C(5) disclosing an investigation report`                                      THEN `single` 125000 3     0 FALSE
    WHEN `s 101C(6) receiving an investigation report knowing it was disclosed in breach`    THEN `single`  50000 2     0 FALSE
    WHEN `s 101R(1) a solicitor failing to name a privileged communicant`                    THEN `single`  50000 2  5000 FALSE
    WHEN `s 101R(2) failing an examination, entry or warrant requirement`                    THEN `single`  50000 2     0 FALSE
    WHEN `s 101R(3) failing to sign the record or keep copy conditions`                      THEN `single`   5000 1     0 FALSE
    WHEN `s 101R(4) failing to produce books under s 101L`                                   THEN `single`  50000 2  5000 FALSE
    WHEN `s 101R(5) false information in an investigation`                                   THEN `single`  50000 2     0 FALSE
    WHEN `s 101R(7) concealing or destroying books under investigation`                      THEN `single` 100000 2     0 FALSE
    WHEN `s 101R(8) obstructing the Authority`                                               THEN `single`  50000 2     0 FALSE
    WHEN `s 101R(9) an occupier failing to give facilities`                                  THEN `single`   5000 1     0 FALSE
    WHEN `s 103(10) acting after an appointment is revoked under statutory management`       THEN `single` 125000 3 12500 FALSE
    WHEN `s 105(2) failing to give information to a statutory manager`                       THEN `single` 125000 3 12500 FALSE
    WHEN `s 119(4) a transferee failing a direction on the auditor's statement`              THEN `single` 100000 0     0 TRUE 
    WHEN `s 124(2) failing to give information under Part 3AA`                               THEN `single` 125000 3 12500 FALSE

§§ `The maximum for this offender (ss 142(5), 143)`

-- s 143(1): "where a corporation is convicted of an offence under this Act,
-- the penalty that the court may impose is a fine not exceeding 2 times the
-- maximum amount that the court could, but for this subsection, impose as a
-- fine for that offence". (2): not "(a) in respect of the breach of a duty
-- imposed only on corporations; or (b) for which different penalties are
-- prescribed ... for individuals and for other persons". FORK F2: the
-- continuing daily fine is "a fine for that offence" too, and is doubled.
-- A person neither an individual nor a corporation (a firm) takes the
-- "any other case" figure, undoubled.
@ref ss 143(1)-(2)
GIVEN o IS AN `IA offence`, individual IS A BOOLEAN, corporation IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `IA penalty`
`the maximum penalty for` o `, an individual:` individual `, a corporation:` corporation MEANS
    IF individual
    THEN `IA penalty` OF (s's `individual fine`), (s's `individual imprisonment, years`), (s's `individual fine per day continuing`)
    ELSE `IA penalty` OF (`factor` TIMES s's `other fine`), 0, (`factor` TIMES s's `other fine per day continuing`)
    WHERE
        s MEANS `the penalty schedule for` o
        `factor` MEANS
            IF corporation AND (NOT s's `split by the person`) AND (NOT s's `a duty only on corporations`)
            THEN 2 ELSE 1

-- s 142(4): an officer of a convicting corporation is guilty too, unless he
-- or she proves due diligence; (5): for a duty imposed only on corporations,
-- the officer is liable "to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 2 years in
-- addition to or in substitution for any fine"; s 143(3): no doubling.
@ref ss 142(4)-(5), 143(3)
GIVEN o IS AN `IA offence`, diligence IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `IA penalty`
`the maximum penalty for an officer of the convicted corporation, for` o `, due diligence proved:` diligence MEANS
    IF diligence THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (`IA penalty` OF (s's `individual fine`), `years`, (s's `individual fine per day continuing`))
    WHERE
        s MEANS `the penalty schedule for` o
        `years` MEANS IF s's `a duty only on corporations` AND s's `individual imprisonment, years` LESS THAN 2
                      THEN 2 ELSE s's `individual imprisonment, years`

§§ `Composition (s 142(7)-(9))`

-- s 142(7): the Authority "may compound any offence under this Act which is
-- prescribed as a compoundable offence by collecting ... a sum of money not
-- exceeding one half of the amount of the maximum fine that is prescribed for
-- that offence". FORK F3: the prescribed fine for the kind of person, before
-- any doubling under s 143.
@ref s 142(7)-(9)
GIVEN o IS AN `IA offence`, individual IS A BOOLEAN, prescribed IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the most that may be collected to compound` o `, an individual:` individual `, prescribed:` prescribed MEANS
    IF NOT prescribed THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST ((IF individual THEN s's `individual fine` ELSE s's `other fine`) DIVIDED BY 2)
    WHERE
        s MEANS `the penalty schedule for` o

§§ `Courts and reach (ss 144, 145)`

-- s 144: "a District Court and a Magistrate's Court have jurisdiction to try
-- any offence under this Act and have power to impose the full penalty".
@ref s 144
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`the courts that may try an offence and impose the full penalty` MEANS
    LIST "a District Court", "a Magistrate's Court"

-- s 145(1): an act "partly in and partly outside Singapore" is treated as done
-- wholly in Singapore. (2): an act outside Singapore "which has a substantial
-- and reasonably foreseeable effect in Singapore" and would be an offence
-- "under section 4, 8, 70 or 75" if done here, is treated as done here.
@ref s 145(1)-(2)
GIVEN p IS A `Place of the act`, `under s 4, 8, 70 or 75` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act reaches an act` p `, an offence under s 4, 8, 70 or 75:` `under s 4, 8, 70 or 75` IF
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN `wholly in Singapore`                                                      THEN TRUE
    WHEN `partly in and partly outside Singapore`                                   THEN TRUE
    WHEN `outside Singapore, with a substantial and reasonably foreseeable effect in Singapore` THEN `under s 4, 8, 70 or 75`
    WHEN `outside Singapore, with no such effect`                                   THEN FALSE
